itle": "payments-api errors after v5.1.0 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v5.0.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-api v5.1.0 left the service unhealthy, with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The service was rolled back in all production regions to v5.0.0, the most recent release marked healthy in production. Needs follow-up: confirm error rates recover and find the root cause in v5.1.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LnA333KhLKULhYYpP7fgCd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service named `payments`. The affected one is **payments-api**. It was on v5.1.0 in all regions, unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. I also tried `payments-service`, which doesn't exist. I didn't check for any other payments services.\n- **Rollback:** v5.1.0 is the only release after v5.0.0 in the history, and it's marked degraded. v5.0.0 was the latest release marked healthy in production, so I rolled payments-api back to it in us-east, us-west and eu-west. A follow-up check shows it healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for payments-api, which paged on-call. It records the bad v5.1.0 deploy and the rollback, and asks for follow-up to confirm the service stays recovered and to find the root cause in v5.1.0.", "type": "text"}]}]}